⍝ Runs every test suite (Tests/*Tests.apln) against APLSource.
⍝
⍝ Usage: dyalogscript Tests/run.apls
⍝
⍝ Exits with code 1 if a file fails to load, or any test fails or errors.

⎕IO ⎕ML←1


findFiles←{{⍵[⍋⍵]}⊆⊃0(⎕NINFO⍠1)⍵}

SOURCE_TYPES←'.apln' '.aplc' '.apli' '.aplf' '.aplo'
isSourceFile←{(⊂3⊃1 ⎕NPARTS ⍵)∊SOURCE_TYPES}

fail←{⍬⊣⍞←'LOAD  ',⍺,': ',⍵,⎕UCS 10}

loadFile←{
    ⍝ ⍺ ←→ ⎕FIX mode: 1 (default) returns a reference to the single
    ⍝      namespace in the file; 2 also accepts functions and operators
    ⍝      and returns the names it established
    ⍝ ← ←→ result of ⎕FIX, or ⍬ when the file fails to load
    ⍺←1
    0::⍵ fail⊃⎕DMX.DM
    r←⍺ ⎕FIX'file://',⍵
    ⍝ 2 ⎕FIX reports some compile errors by establishing nothing
    ⍝ rather than by signalling.
    0≠≢r:r
    ⍵ fail'nothing was established'
}

args←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
test_dir←⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃args
root←⊃1 ⎕NPARTS ¯1↓test_dir

⍝ Suites are loaded before everything else, so a suite that uses another
⍝ namespace while it is being fixed fails here, whatever order Link or
⍝ a session would load the files in. Such an error is reported but
⍝ leaves the suite incomplete, so its tests then fail.
⍝ The suites are fixed in a :Trap at script level: an error in a
⍝ multi-line dfn called during the fix escapes a dfn error guard and
⍝ leaves the script running inside the suite.
suites←⍬
:For path :In findFiles test_dir,'*Tests.apln'
    :Trap 0
        suites,←⎕FIX'file://',path
    :Else
        _←path fail⊃⎕DMX.DM
        suites,←⊂⍬
    :EndTrap
:EndFor

paths←findFiles root,'APLSource/*'
sources←2 loadFile¨(isSourceFile¨paths)/paths
support←loadFile¨test_dir∘,¨'Tester.apln' 'Assert.apln' 'Helpers.apln'
failed←∨/0=≢¨sources,support,suites

:if ~failed
    suites←(0≠≢¨suites)/suites
    results←Tester.run suites
    failed∨←Tester.failed results
:endIf

⎕OFF(failed)
